#Image Compression using Principal Component Analysis (PCA)

An unsupervised machine learning implementation demonstrating dimensionality reduction and image compression using **Principal Component Analysis (PCA)** in python


##Overview

In this project, a greyscale image is treated as a 2D numerical matrix where each row represents an observation and each column represents a feature, By applying PCA,
the high-dimensional pixel data is projected onto a lower-dimensional subspace of principal components that retain the maximum variance, allowing the image to be reconstructed
with significantly fewer stored values

## Workflow & MEthodology

1 "Data Loading & Preprocessing": Loads the standard '512 x 512' grayscale *Cameraman* dataset from 'sckit-image' and converts pixel intensties to floating-point values
2 "Variance Analysis": fits a full 512 components PCa model to evaluate individual and cumulative explained variance ratios

